<section class="band band-soft">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Research, right now</h2>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p>2026 has been a year of hard lessons and real leads. Every randomised trial presented for the first time at the Berlin conference in May missed its main goal. But in several of those trials, <strong>some patients clearly responded</strong>. Researchers are now picking patients by biomarker, so the right treatment can be tested on the right people.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Brain waste clearance:</strong> Griffith University showed for the first time that ME/CFS impairs the brain's overnight "clean-up" system, which is linked to brain fog.</li>
          <li><strong>Genes:</strong> DecodeME found eight genetic signals, mainly in the immune and nervous systems.</li>
          <li><strong>Promising leads:</strong> low-dose rapamycin, bezisterim in PEM-heavy patients, and B-cell and plasma-cell therapies in autoimmune subgroups.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><a class="btn" href="/research/results/">What worked and what didn't</a></p>
      </div>
