<section class="band band-soft">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="how-to-read-this-site">How to read this site</h2>
    <p>ME/CFS attracts a lot of hope, and a lot of hype. So that you can judge each claim for yourself, we label it with the kind of evidence behind it:</p>
    <ul class="ev-legend">
      <li>{% ev "rct" %} Randomised, placebo-controlled trial. The strongest kind.</li>
      <li>{% ev "controlled" %} Has a comparison group, but isn't fully randomised or blinded.</li>
      <li>{% ev "open" %} No placebo group. Everyone knows what they're getting.</li>
      <li>{% ev "observational" %} Watches patients without assigning a treatment.</li>
      <li>{% ev "lab" %} Cells in a dish. Not proof that it helps people.</li>
      <li>{% ev "adjacent" %} Evidence from Long COVID, POTS or fibromyalgia, not ME/CFS directly.</li>
      <li>{% ev "hypothesis" %} A proposed idea that hasn't been tested yet.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">Why this matters: in fatigue illnesses, 20–40% of people (sometimes more) feel better on a sugar pill. A treatment "helping 80% of people" in a study with no placebo group can mean very little.</p>
  </div>
</section>
